    {
      "section": "General Aptitude",
      "text": "What is the unit digit of the expression \\((7^{95} - 3^{58})\\)?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "2",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "4",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "6",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "8",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Shortcut (Cyclicity Method): The unit digits of powers of 7 repeat in a cycle of 4: 7, 9, 3, 1. For \\(7^{95}\\), divide exponent by 4: \\(95 \\bmod 4 = 3\\), so unit digit is the 3rd in cycle = 3. The unit digits of powers of 3 repeat in a cycle of 4: 3, 9, 7, 1. For \\(3^{58}\\), \\(58 \\bmod 4 = 2\\), so unit digit is the 2nd in cycle = 9. Since 3 < 9, borrow 10: \\(13 - 9 = 4\\). Step-by-step: \\(7^1=7, 7^2=49, 7^3=343, 7^4=2401\\) → cycle (7,9,3,1). \\(95 = 4 \\times 23 + 3\\) → unit digit of \\(7^{95}\\) is 3. \\(3^1=3, 3^2=9, 3^3=27, 3^4=81\\) → cycle (3,9,7,1). \\(58 = 4 \\times 14 + 2\\) → unit digit of \\(3^{58}\\) is 9. Unit digit of difference = \\((10+3) - 9 = 4\\).",
      "topic": "Number System - Unit Digit & Cyclicity",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "source": "model",
      "model": "qwen3.5:9b",
      "generatedAt": "2026-11-14T22:09:09.889Z",
      "reviewed": false,
